Linux kernel, https://git.kernel.org (GPL-2.0)
  Releases ship a kernel inside the boot images techo5-boot-<version>.img (Echo Show 5 2nd gen,
  cronos) and techo5-boot-checkers-<version>.img (1st gen, checkers): Linux 4.9.337 for arm64. It is
  GPL-2.0, and this is where its source is.
    - Source: github.com/amazon-oss/android_kernel_amazon_mt8163, branch cronos/lineage-18.1, at
      commit 8d928c5176cc — the commit the LineageOS 18.1 boot image was built from (`uname -r` on
      the unit is 4.9.337-g8d928c5176cc). One commit serves both generations; the 1st gen has its own
      device trees in the same tree.
    - Configuration: cronos_defconfig for the 2nd gen, checkers_defconfig for the 1st, from that
      tree, with Bluetooth added. The resulting configurations are recorded in
      docs/dumps/cronos-lineage-kernel-4.9.337.config (as LineageOS ships it) and
      docs/dumps/cronos-techo5-kernel-4.9.337-bt.config (as TECHO5 builds it);
      docs/dumps/cronos-twrp-kernel-4.9.77.config is the TWRP kernel's, for comparison. All three are
      derived from that GPL-2.0 source and are GPL-2.0 themselves.
    - Changes: the patches in tools/linux/patches, applied for the 1st gen Show 5 and Show 8 builds.
      checkers-0001-mic-enable-on-capture.patch changes drivers/misc/gating.c, include/misc/gating.h
      and sound/soc/mediatek/mt_soc_audio_8163_amzn/mt_soc_machine.c so that releasing the mute
      latch brings the microphone path back; checkers-0002-camera-follows-the-latch.patch changes
      drivers/misc/gating.c and the checkers and crown kd_camera_hw.c so the camera follows the
      latch; checkers-0003-mute-button-follows-a-short-press.patch changes drivers/misc/gating.c so
      a short press that releases the latch is not missed; checkers-0004-jack-plugged-in-at-boot.patch
      changes drivers/misc/mediatek/accdet/mt8163/accdet_amzn.c so a plug in the headphone jack at
      power-on no longer stops the boot. They are modifications of that GPL-2.0
      source, so they are GPL-2.0 too. The appended device trees then have amzn,mic-downmix removed
      (tools/linux/patch-dtb.py).
    - The script that does all of it is tools/linux/build-kernel.sh, and docs/building.md is how to
      run it. A rebuild reproduces the shipped kernel.

