Linux kernel patches for the Echo Show 8 2nd gen, tools/linux/athena/kernel
  Patches to Linux 6.18.56, the board device tree and an ALSA machine driver (based on MediaTek's
  mt8183-mt6358-ts3a227-max98357.c), all GPL-2.0 like the kernel (the device tree GPL-2.0 OR MIT).
  The panel init tables in patches/panel are taken from Amazon's GPL-2.0 kernel for the device
  (the sequences its LCM drivers send).
  The camera drivers in src/camera/isp (MediaTek's sensor interface and CAMSV, from BayLibre's
  MT8365 ISP 3.0 series with MT8183 support) are from https://github.com/vpavlin/mt8183-camera,
  GPL-2.0, with their copyright and SPDX headers kept; the changes are marked "athena:". The
  OV13855 driver in src/camera is new, GPL-2.0; its register tables (ov13855-tables.inc) are from
  Rockchip's GPL-2.0 driver (drivers/media/i2c/ov13855.c in rockchip-linux/kernel, develop-6.1,
  Copyright (C) 2021 Rockchip Electronics Co., Ltd.).
  In the boot image built from them the kernel is under the GPL-2.0. MediaTek's MT7663 Wi-Fi and
  Bluetooth firmware, from linux-firmware, is not linked into the kernel: it ships as separate
  files in the boot image's ramdisk (lib/firmware), under MediaTek's own license, whose text
  (LICENCE.mediatek) is in the ramdisk with them.
  Releases ship it as Linux 6.18.56 for arm64 in techo5-boot-athena-<version>.img; its source is
  published with each release as linux-6.18.56-techo5-athena-<version>-source.tar.xz. The panel
  picker, src/panel/panel-athena-select.c (GPL-2.0), is TECHO5's own: it chooses the unit's screen
  from the name the bootloader passes.

Linux kernel for the Skylight Calendar 15, tools/linux/skylight/kernel
  Releases ship Linux 6.18.56 for arm64 in techo5-boot-skylight-<version>.img and the installer
  image techo5-installer-skylight-<version>.img, under the GPL-2.0. Its source is published with each
  release as linux-6.18.56-techo5-skylight-<version>-source.tar.xz: the kernel.org tree with the board
  files, the panel driver and the build's configuration (techo5-skylight.config) in it.
  The board device tree, rk3566-skylight-cal150.dts ((GPL-2.0+ OR MIT), like the kernel's Rockchip
  trees), is TECHO5's, with its PMIC layout following rk3566-bigtreetech-cb2.dtsi and its display path
  rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi from the kernel's own tree. Its values, and the panel driver's
  (panel-skylight-cal150.c, GPL-2.0) 38 bridge init writes and timing, are taken from the unit's stock
  device tree.
  The Wi-Fi and Bluetooth firmware is not shipped: each unit's own goes into its store at install,
  from its vendor partition.

Light sensor, echod/internal/hardware/ambient/em3071x.go
  The Everlight EM3071X's register addresses and the value that switches it on are the ones Rockchip's
