FFmpeg, https://ffmpeg.org (LGPL-2.1-or-later)
  Every root filesystem carries ffmpeg 8.1.2 for the video player and live cameras as
  /usr/local/bin/techo5-ffmpeg (armv7). The Echo Show 8 2nd gen (athena) and Skylight Calendar root
  filesystems and stores also carry it as /usr/local/bin/techo5-ffmpeg64 (aarch64, statically linked),
  with the H.265, VP8 and VP9 decoders added. Both are built under the LGPL only: no --enable-gpl, no
  --enable-nonfree.
    - Source: ffmpeg's release tarball, https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-8.1.2.tar.xz (its SHA-256 is
      in the build scripts).
    - Changes: one, to libavformat/rtsp.c, so an RTSP camera's Basic login is ignored rather than
      answered with the password in the clear. It is a modification of that LGPL source, so it is
      LGPL-2.1-or-later too. The patch and the configure flags are in tools/linux/build-ffmpeg.sh.
    - Build: tools/linux/build-ffmpeg.sh (armv7) and tools/linux/build-ffmpeg-arm64.sh (aarch64), and
      docs/building.md is how to run them. They rebuild the shipped binaries from the source above, and
      the binaries can be relinked or replaced the same way.
  The armv7 build uses the root filesystem's own Alpine OpenSSL and zlib libraries. The aarch64 build
  has these linked into it, all from Alpine Linux v3.24's aarch64 packages, unmodified: musl (MIT
  License), OpenSSL 3 (Apache License 2.0), zlib (zlib License) and GCC's libgcc (GPL-3.0 with the GCC
  Runtime Library Exception). Their sources are Alpine's,
  https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports/-/tree/3.24-stable. The build prints the versions it
  used; the first release's were musl 1.2.6-r2, openssl-libs-static 3.5.9-r0, zlib-static 1.3.2-r1
  and libgcc 15.2.0-r5.
  Its license files are in every root filesystem, /usr/share/licenses/ffmpeg.

